{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.WignerSU4RowBoundInactive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.WignerSU4RowBoundInactive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su4_active_at_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su4_active_at_five","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L158-L164","doc":"**The bound is genuine, and first bites at `n = 5`.**  `[1⁵]` has five rows, so it\nis not SU(4)-admissible — the `dim [1ⁿ] = C(4,n) = 0` for `n ≥ 5` fact the corpus uses\nto locate the turnover.  Together with `su4_inactive_of_le_four` this pins the\nactivation threshold exactly at `n = 5`: the constraint is real, and it is real\nstrictly *above* the range where the ⁴He enhancement is claimed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.rows_allOnes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.rows_allOnes","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L155-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.allOnes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.allOnes","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L146-L153","doc":"The all-ones partition of `n`, used to show the SU(4) bound is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su4_no_magic_enhancement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su4_no_magic_enhancement","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L120-L133","doc":"**The enhancement statement.**  The SU(4) row restriction takes the *same* value —\nnamely, no value at all: the unrestricted sum — at `n = 3` and at `n = 4`, for every\nweight.  So it cannot be the source of a factor present at ⁴He and absent at the `A = 3`\npair.  This is the formal content of \"SU(4) LOCATES the `A = 4` turnover but does not\nSIZE it\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su4_restricted_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su4_restricted_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L109-L118","doc":"**The exclusion.**  For every `n ≤ 4` and every weight function `w` into any\n`AddCommMonoid`, the SU(4)-restricted Schur–Weyl sum coincides with the unrestricted\none.  Imposing SU(4) admissibility below `n = 5` changes nothing, whatever is being\nsummed — in particular it cannot introduce a factor at `A = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su4_filter_eq_univ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su4_filter_eq_univ","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L101-L107","doc":"Restated as a set identity: below `n = 5` the SU(4)-admissible partitions are *all*\nthe partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su4_inactive_of_le_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su4_inactive_of_le_four","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**The bound is inactive below 5.**  For `n ≤ 4` every partition of `n` is SU(4)\nadmissible, since it has at most `n ≤ 4` rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.instDecidableSU4Admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.instDecidableSU4Admissible","kind":"instance","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SU4Admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SU4Admissible","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L88-L90","doc":"Wigner SU(4) admissibility: the spin–isospin space is 4-dimensional, so a Young\ndiagram carries a nonzero SU(4) irrep exactly when it has at most 4 rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.rows_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.rows_le","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L80-L86","doc":"**The invariant.**  A partition of `n` has at most `n` rows, because every part is\npositive.  This is the whole content of the file: everything below is a consequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_le_sum_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_le_sum_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L67-L78","doc":"A multiset of positive naturals has at most as many elements as its sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.rows","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WignerSU4RowBoundInactive.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The number of **rows** of a partition — the number of its parts.  In the Wigner\nsupermultiplet reading this is the number of rows of the Young diagram, and SU(4)\nadmissibility is the requirement that it not exceed `dim` of the spin–isospin space. ","signatureChunk":0}]}